      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Congenital factor V deficiency is an uncommon bleeding disorder that necessitates hemostatic correction before surgery. We herein describe a patient with severe factor V deficiency who underwent successful off-pump coronary artery bypass grafting with a transfusion of fresh-frozen plasma."},
